{"id": "EUVD-2026-93104", "enisaUuid": "27396837-7924-3432-9930-b7763ce1b4f7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Avoid integer underflow with ffs in EOP ring size calc\n\nThe low 6 bits of cp_hqd_eop_control store the base-2 logarithm\nof the EOP ring size. This was calculated as\n\nffs(q->eop_ring_buffer_size / sizeof(unsigned int)) - 1 - 1\n\nBut ffs can in theory return 1 or 0, so this could underflow\n(although in practice the ring buffer size cannot be less than 4096).\n\nChange this to\n\nffs(q->eop_ring_buffer_size / sizeof(unsigned int) / 4)\n\nusing properties of logarithms.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4f18c56630383c14bfc6b2d65f88f2f895d2121a)", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/82e1b8299c6da02ce02185c208d2fdf7572b5ea1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c883d0a132d430ef7ebb23fd94323be94d0fbdb8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mv47-6r4w-p28q", "CVE-2026-98176"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c346f14-c4b8-352f-8823-3511b087fb08", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "136dc274-e683-32c9-9e66-32e0eac453b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "14328aa58ce523a59996c5a82681c43ec048cc33 <c883d0a132d430ef7ebb23fd94323be94d0fbdb8"}, {"id": "213f6511-f731-3b02-b6e4-4ca46c503aea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "14328aa58ce523a59996c5a82681c43ec048cc33 <82e1b8299c6da02ce02185c208d2fdf7572b5ea1"}, {"id": "574c9c59-f061-3ceb-a061-6c2f2a902347", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "86a27505-4ca2-3ba1-8829-e61412860c52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "c72cab6b-6cc3-3883-9d34-4180111a2ae1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c2f10a17-50bc-31b6-9d13-8e2746133ce2", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}